; Michael (v2), the Ben Eater-style 65C02 board: the emulator's `--machine michael`
; (emulator/README.md), run with no ROM image and the program loaded into RAM with
; `--load 2000`. lathe/docs/boards.md has the whole recipe.
;
; RAM is $0000-$3FFF; the VIA is at $6000 (the LCD is on its ports). Without a ROM the
; emulator points reset at the load address and the IRQ vector at $3F00, where a program
; that wants interrupts stores `JMP handler`; so code stops at $3EFF. There are no host
; services: a program shows its output on the 20x4 LCD and ends with STP, which ends the run.
cpu       65c02
zeropage  $00 $FF
code      $2000 $3EFF
data      $0200 $1FFF
stack     $FF
exit      stop
output    raw         ; the file is the code from $2000, and the load address is $start
